hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18098","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar from a shaykh he named from Nuaym ibn al-Nahham, he said: I heard the caller of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a cold night while I was in my blanket, then I wished that he would say: Pray in your dwellings, then when he reached: Come to success, he said: Pray in your dwellings. Then I asked about it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had commanded him with that."
"18099","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban informed me from Nuaym ibn al-Nahham, he said: Dawn was called on a cold day while I was in the cloak of my wife, then I said: Would that the caller said: Whoever stayed, no blame upon him. Then the caller of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called at the end of his call: And whoever stayed, no blame upon him."
